Exercise 6.1
The code will print "Different text" as the == compares two variables. Instead of using ==, use .equals() is better as it compares the contents of the string variable.
The corrected code:
String first = new String("Java");
String second = new String("Java");

if (first.equals(second)) {
    System.out.println("Same text");
} else {
    System.out.println("Different text");
}

